WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:03.286
- This ain't Arby's, but we got the meats.

00:00:03.286 --> 00:00:06.036
(big band music)

00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:10.523
Hey, what's up?

00:00:10.523 --> 00:00:11.436
It's Tway, and welcome to "Making it Big,"

00:00:11.436 --> 00:00:14.820
the show where I take your favorite foods

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:17.490
and turn it into giant foods.

00:00:17.490 --> 00:00:20.850
For this season, we are
actually filming everything

00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:22.650
with a VR camera.

00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:26.001
So if you notice that my
table is a little warped,

00:00:26.001 --> 00:00:27.120
that's why.

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:28.890
You can watch the full VR episode

00:00:28.890 --> 00:00:31.290
with a Meta Quest 2 in Mega Tasty.

00:00:31.290 --> 00:00:34.170
That's our virtual cooking
world within Horizon World

00:00:34.170 --> 00:00:35.940
or on Meta Quest TV.

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:40.788
So today I have a special guest
that you all know and love.

00:00:40.788 --> 00:00:41.743
(regal horn music)

00:00:41.743 --> 00:00:44.610
- I'm here, hello, hello!

00:00:44.610 --> 00:00:49.440
- You guys, it is Rie, Queen of "Tasty."

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:51.180
I gotta admit, I'm kind of nervous.

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:52.013
- Oh, why?

00:00:52.013 --> 00:00:56.520
- You are challenging me
because your taste is expansive,

00:00:56.520 --> 00:00:59.790
and I don't know what you are
going to be challenging me to,

00:00:59.790 --> 00:01:02.400
because you are kind of unpredictable.

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:05.490
- Well, you know I have a
show called "Make It Fancy,"

00:01:05.490 --> 00:01:09.305
but you might be surprised
what I chose. (laughs)

00:01:09.305 --> 00:01:10.727
- Okay, let's see.

00:01:10.727 --> 00:01:11.560
- Tada!

00:01:13.410 --> 00:01:14.610
- Korean cheese dog.

00:01:14.610 --> 00:01:17.160
- Yeah, far from fancy,
it's a street food.

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:18.900
I'm new to Korean cheese dog.

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:19.733
- Yeah.

00:01:19.733 --> 00:01:21.480
- But I love it.

00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:23.550
So I just wanna eat more.

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:25.560
And why not make it big so I can eat more?

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:27.300
- Why not, right?

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:30.120
What is your favorite part
about the Korean cheese dog?

00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:32.400
- You know, I'm a "Tasty" producer

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:35.130
and we love good cheese pull.

00:01:35.130 --> 00:01:35.963
- Yeah, yes.

00:01:35.963 --> 00:01:40.050
- So I expect you to do great cheese pull.

00:01:40.050 --> 00:01:44.790
The stretch is from at least here to here.

00:01:44.790 --> 00:01:48.000
I don't think I can do
it, but I believe in you.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:49.290
I think you can do it.

00:01:49.290 --> 00:01:50.310
Good luck, friend.

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:51.153
- Thank you.

00:01:53.523 --> 00:01:54.963
Let's get to work.

00:01:56.026 --> 00:01:58.776
(big band music)

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:04.030
So I have five pounds of
ground beef over here.

00:02:04.030 --> 00:02:08.670
This is a pound and a
half of ground pork belly.

00:02:08.670 --> 00:02:09.993
Gonna mix this up.

00:02:11.430 --> 00:02:12.810
Oh hey!

00:02:12.810 --> 00:02:15.060
Okay, well, Tiny Tway is
here and it looks like

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:16.320
she got sumpn' to say.

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:17.940
So let's hear it.

00:02:17.940 --> 00:02:19.350
No way.

00:02:19.350 --> 00:02:20.850
That long?

00:02:20.850 --> 00:02:22.700
According to Tiny Tway, the corn dog

00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:26.583
got really popular in Korea in 1980.

00:02:26.583 --> 00:02:27.990
- [Official-Sounding
Announcer] In the 1980s.

00:02:27.990 --> 00:02:32.070
- But it wasn't until 2016
where it gained its popularity

00:02:32.070 --> 00:02:35.940
because they like basically
rebranded the corn dog

00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:39.990
and added like the sugar and
the cheese and all the sauces,

00:02:39.990 --> 00:02:43.410
and now it's literally
everywhere in the world.

00:02:43.410 --> 00:02:48.410
So for flavoring, I have, I
think this is onion powder.

00:02:48.870 --> 00:02:50.790
No, this is onion powder.

00:02:50.790 --> 00:02:52.860
This is garlic powder.

00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:54.813
This is white pepper.

00:02:55.950 --> 00:02:59.310
Oh, don't breathe that white pepper in.

00:02:59.310 --> 00:03:01.110
This is paprika.

00:03:01.110 --> 00:03:05.160
And this right here is pink curing salt.

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:10.160
So what pink curing salt is is
just salt and sodium nitrate?

00:03:12.750 --> 00:03:13.583
All right.

00:03:16.710 --> 00:03:19.890
I like to feel it kind of like squeeze

00:03:19.890 --> 00:03:22.362
through my fingers, and make sure

00:03:22.362 --> 00:03:27.183
that every inch of this
meat is covered with flavor.

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:31.950
Oh, this meat smells seasoned.

00:03:31.950 --> 00:03:35.700
Now I am ready to make this into a paste

00:03:35.700 --> 00:03:38.419
because we're making a hot dog here.

00:03:38.419 --> 00:03:42.030
(processor grinds)

00:03:42.030 --> 00:03:43.893
Look at our beautiful paste.

00:03:45.420 --> 00:03:47.160
Okay, that was only one batch.

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:51.060
I have this much left to do.

00:03:51.060 --> 00:03:52.983
So be right back.

00:03:53.827 --> 00:03:56.520
(easy rhythmic music)

00:03:56.520 --> 00:03:58.920
This is not a hot dog casing,

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:02.280
because we can't find any
that's actually this big.

00:04:02.280 --> 00:04:06.989
So this is like a, a casing for salami.

00:04:06.989 --> 00:04:08.430
(casing crinkles)

00:04:08.430 --> 00:04:09.263
Here we go.

00:04:13.134 --> 00:04:15.890
What I gotta do is really
make sure (container taps)

00:04:15.890 --> 00:04:17.680
that there are no air bubbles.

00:04:17.680 --> 00:04:19.340
(container pounding on counter)

00:04:19.340 --> 00:04:20.173
(casing crunches)

00:04:20.173 --> 00:04:21.006
(more pounding)

00:04:21.006 --> 00:04:23.850
I don't want (more
pounding) any air bubbles.

00:04:23.850 --> 00:04:25.037
That's the enemy.

00:04:25.037 --> 00:04:26.571
(ominous electronic chord)

00:04:26.571 --> 00:04:29.730
(melodic electronic music)

00:04:29.730 --> 00:04:32.130
So we've already tied the other end.

00:04:32.130 --> 00:04:34.933
I'm going to, ugh- (laughs)

00:04:36.720 --> 00:04:39.933
This is my foot long glizzy.

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:43.170
And this is going into the oven

00:04:43.170 --> 00:04:47.610
for an hour and a half at 300 degrees.

00:04:47.610 --> 00:04:51.330
This is going to cook the
hot dog and let it firm up.

00:04:51.330 --> 00:04:52.833
So, be right back.

00:04:53.673 --> 00:04:56.670
(relaxed retro music)

00:04:56.670 --> 00:05:00.573
This is our boiled hotdog.

00:05:02.310 --> 00:05:07.310
I'm gonna cut this side so you can see it.

00:05:07.406 --> 00:05:10.470
(drum boings)

00:05:10.470 --> 00:05:12.651
Children look away.

00:05:12.651 --> 00:05:15.318
(sensual music)

00:05:19.422 --> 00:05:20.255
(needle sliding on record)

00:05:20.255 --> 00:05:22.290
Okay. So I actually need
to put this in the oven

00:05:22.290 --> 00:05:27.180
at 500 for 15 minutes because
I want this to crisp up,

00:05:27.180 --> 00:05:30.630
get a nice color going
because I mean, he's great,

00:05:30.630 --> 00:05:32.253
but he could be better.

00:05:33.210 --> 00:05:34.460
So let's make him better.

00:05:35.432 --> 00:05:38.970
(rock and roll beat)

00:05:38.970 --> 00:05:41.400
My meat is done. (sniffing)

00:05:41.400 --> 00:05:43.140
It smells incredible.

00:05:43.140 --> 00:05:48.140
Now we get to shave the
cheese nice and tight.

00:05:49.641 --> 00:05:54.224
(driving rock and roll beat continues)

00:05:55.386 --> 00:05:58.719
(funky sax joins music)

00:05:59.910 --> 00:06:02.040
What we're gonna do is put this stick

00:06:02.040 --> 00:06:06.060
through the dog, because this is going

00:06:06.060 --> 00:06:08.490
to hold the cheese and the dog together,

00:06:08.490 --> 00:06:10.590
but it's also like the stick

00:06:10.590 --> 00:06:14.040
to hold the whole thing
together when you're eating it.

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:15.055
Here we go.

00:06:15.055 --> 00:06:17.888
(music continues)

00:06:19.137 --> 00:06:20.970
It went through!

00:06:20.970 --> 00:06:24.510
I am going to actually
use these little skewers

00:06:24.510 --> 00:06:29.040
to secure this to this
because it's so big.

00:06:29.040 --> 00:06:32.492
I can't trust just one stick, you know?

00:06:32.492 --> 00:06:34.256
(suspenseful music begins)

00:06:34.256 --> 00:06:37.653
So I am going to secure it
with these stick right here.

00:06:39.870 --> 00:06:44.870
All right, now time to put this together.

00:06:45.546 --> 00:06:46.379
I-

00:06:47.424 --> 00:06:48.257
Ooh

00:06:49.230 --> 00:06:50.460
I need some help.

00:06:50.460 --> 00:06:51.439
Beryl (echoes)?

00:06:51.439 --> 00:06:54.605
(drum roll)

00:06:54.605 --> 00:06:56.977
I'm gonna put my hand here to guide.

00:06:56.977 --> 00:07:00.144
(drum roll continues)

00:07:03.019 --> 00:07:04.371
(sticks crunch)

00:07:04.371 --> 00:07:07.770
(funky organ music)

00:07:07.770 --> 00:07:10.550
Time for the batter.

00:07:10.550 --> 00:07:13.383
(music continues)

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:24.120
Oh hey, welcome back.

00:07:24.120 --> 00:07:25.323
Okay, let's hear it.

00:07:27.300 --> 00:07:29.400
So, according to Tiny Tway,

00:07:29.400 --> 00:07:32.490
the difference between a Korean corn dog

00:07:32.490 --> 00:07:33.323
and a traditional American corn dog

00:07:33.323 --> 00:07:38.323
is that the batter for American
corn dolls have cornmeal,

00:07:38.760 --> 00:07:41.227
but the Korean one does not.

00:07:41.227 --> 00:07:45.720
So that's why there's no
cornmeal in this corn dog matter.

00:07:45.720 --> 00:07:46.923
The more you know.

00:07:46.923 --> 00:07:50.590
(ethereal musical flourish)

00:07:52.770 --> 00:07:54.150
It's game time.

00:07:54.150 --> 00:07:59.150
So I have to get the
glizzy coated in flour,

00:07:59.280 --> 00:08:01.320
and then I'm gonna bring it over here

00:08:01.320 --> 00:08:05.373
and batter it and then coat it in panko.

00:08:06.444 --> 00:08:09.111
(playful music)

00:08:21.565 --> 00:08:23.315
A little glizzy ASMR.

00:08:26.610 --> 00:08:27.443
The tingles!

00:08:27.443 --> 00:08:31.062
(playful, mysterious music)

00:08:32.146 --> 00:08:36.150
Okay, welcome to the back kitchen.

00:08:36.150 --> 00:08:38.070
Over there is my fry team.

00:08:38.070 --> 00:08:39.423
Hi, fry team!

00:08:39.423 --> 00:08:40.350
- [Echoing Announcer] Fry guys,

00:08:40.350 --> 00:08:42.773
your guide to anything fried.

00:08:43.650 --> 00:08:45.891
- All right, drop the glizzy.

00:08:45.891 --> 00:08:49.724
(serious rock and roll music)

00:08:55.625 --> 00:08:59.125
(lounge-style jazz music)

00:09:00.300 --> 00:09:02.580
This glizzy is glorious.

00:09:02.580 --> 00:09:04.920
It's looking beautiful.

00:09:04.920 --> 00:09:06.660
Rie, are you here?

00:09:06.660 --> 00:09:07.953
- I am here.

00:09:10.756 --> 00:09:13.320
- [Tway And Rie] Wow!

00:09:13.320 --> 00:09:14.297
- Oh my god.

00:09:15.540 --> 00:09:17.100
You made a box too?

00:09:17.100 --> 00:09:19.032
- Yeah, well I didn't make it.

00:09:19.032 --> 00:09:20.449
- Okay.
- The art- (both laughing)

00:09:20.449 --> 00:09:21.442
- Department.

00:09:21.442 --> 00:09:24.933
- Oh! (laughs) Make it rain.

00:09:26.757 --> 00:09:27.660
- Are you ready?

00:09:27.660 --> 00:09:29.340
- Yeah, three, two, one.

00:09:29.340 --> 00:09:31.350
- [Tway] We love good cheese pull.

00:09:31.350 --> 00:09:32.183
Oh-

00:09:33.487 --> 00:09:37.837
- Aah. (laughs)

00:09:39.390 --> 00:09:41.790
Whoa. It's a lot of cheese.

00:09:41.790 --> 00:09:42.750
- It's pulling.

00:09:42.750 --> 00:09:43.583
- How about this?

00:09:43.583 --> 00:09:44.416
- No, it's pulling.

00:09:45.293 --> 00:09:47.374
(Rie laughs)

00:09:47.374 --> 00:09:49.957
(cosmic music)

00:09:50.940 --> 00:09:54.423
We love good cheese pull.(echoing)

00:10:03.600 --> 00:10:06.413
I was gonna say, should
we put the toppings on?

00:10:06.413 --> 00:10:09.660
(upbeat folk music)

00:10:09.660 --> 00:10:12.033
- Okay, so I'm gonna do cross.

00:10:13.001 --> 00:10:15.390
- This is very precious cargo.

00:10:15.390 --> 00:10:17.488
There's a sriracha shortage.

00:10:17.488 --> 00:10:18.327
- Oh my god.

00:10:18.327 --> 00:10:19.773
- [Tway] Can we cheers?

00:10:19.773 --> 00:10:21.480
- [Rie] Cheers.

00:10:21.480 --> 00:10:22.951
Cheers to Tway.

00:10:22.951 --> 00:10:24.810
(folk music continues)

00:10:24.810 --> 00:10:26.700
Oh, it's yummy.

00:10:26.700 --> 00:10:28.159
It's so good.

00:10:28.159 --> 00:10:30.000
- I actually really enjoyed this

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:31.260
- Mm-hmm.

00:10:31.260 --> 00:10:32.310
- [Tway] In the comments below,

00:10:32.310 --> 00:10:35.820
Let me know what I should
make big next time.

00:10:35.820 --> 00:10:36.990
- Peace.

00:10:36.990 --> 00:10:38.452
